  "visualTeachingNotes": [
    "A person held or framed through the middle, with the center of the body emphasized.",
    "Oracle shows a human-like figure whose torso is caught inside a U-shaped or forked frame, making the middle visually dominant.",
    "Regular 央 tightens those crossing strokes around the center, leaving a character whose visual weight remains concentrated in the middle."
  ],
